0 Fruit bodies large, robust, fleshy, pileus covered with distinct, broad, tomentose to felt-like scales, spores ellipsoid to ovoid, germ pore present. 03101115190 subgen. Hemipholiota (key D) (additional characters: fruit bodies dry, spores with germ pore)28
0 Fruit bodies medium-sized to small, Jess fleshy, scales (if present) small and appressed, spores sub- amygdaliform or distinctly phaseoliform (in side view), germ pore present or absent031012152004
0 Spores suban1ygdaliform in side view, slightly dextrinoid, germ pore small but distinct when carefully observed 04121316210 subgen. Flammula (key C) (additional characters: fruit bodies medium-sized to large. pileus smooth, dry or slightly sticky when moist, margin slightly hygrophanous in damp weather, scales mostly absent)29
