0 Hyaline cheilocystidia (leptocystidia) long and slender, cylindrical or narrowly lageniform, with subcapitate to capitate apex, fruit bodies small to medium-sized (pileus 1-5(-8) cm), pileus with fine scales (up to 0.2 cm broad) or smooth0821222033015
0 Cheilocystidia not so long and slender, apex usually not capitate, fruitbodies medium-sized to large (pile us 3-15(-20) cm), scales present at )east when young or moist, rather distinct, broader than 0.2 cm082123203409
0 Pileus and stipe dry, mat, yellow, yellow-ochre to yellow-rusty, scales distinct, numerous, of fibrillose nature, rusty-ochre to rusty-brown, upturned to appressed, spores (5.8-)6.2-8.2(-9.0) x 3.7-5.0 µm , germ pore distinct. 09232421350 Pholiota squarrosa, pp. 340
0 Other combination of characters. Pileus usually sticky, viscid to glutinous when moist, lustrous when dry0923252136010
0 Pileus centre covered with very distinct, echinate, conical to upturned scales, pileus margin whitish to pale yellow when young, stipe with rough erect scales, spores small, (4.0-)4.5-6.0(-6.5) x (2.5-)2.7-3.5(-4.0) µm, slightly phaseoliform in side view, pale, thin-walled, germ pore absent. 010252622370 Pholiota squarrosoides, pp. 630
0 Pileus and stipe with Jess prominent, non-echinate scales, pileus margin not so pale, spores larger, darker coloured, with germ pore01025272238011
