0 Spores narrower (only exceptionally reaching 5.5 µm but mostly Jess than 5 µm )01127292340013
0 Cheilocystidia of various shape: fusiform, cylindrical, narrowly clavate, narrowly lageniform, obovoid when young, often ail these types present on one edge, pileus strongly glutinous in damp weather, after drying somewhat lustrous, with thin rusty-ochre to rusty-brown scales, spores (7.0-)7.5-10.0(-11.0) x (4.5-)5.0-6.2(-6.5) µm, germ pore 0.8-1.2 µm broad, chrysocystidia scattered to rare; growing mostly on Fagus, but also on other deciduous trees, sometimes on conifers. 012283024410 Pholiota adiposa, pp. 400
0 Cheilocystidia mostly clavate to broadly clavate, pileus slightly viscid in damp weather, other­ wise dry, mat, covered with dark thick scales (almost brown-black when old), spores 7.5-11.0 (-11.5) x 5.0-6.5(-7.0) µm , germ pore very distinct, 1.0-1.5(-1.8) µm broad. chrysocystidia abundant; growing on living and dead trunks and logs of Salix, mostly Salix fragilis. 012283124420 Pholiota cerifera, pp. 470
0 Pileus with numerous, small, dark, rusty-brown to blackish-brown scales, strongly glutinous to viscid when moist, spores (4.5-)5.0-7.0(-7.5) x 3.0-4.0(-4.5) µm , germ pore small, indistinct growing in dense clusters at bases of trunks, on roots or wood buried in soi1. 013293225430 Pholiota jahnii, pp. 580
