0 Growing terrestrial (no connection with wood is visible), pileus margin whitish when young, centre gradually becoming more yellow and finally more or less orange, especially in centre with thin, dark brown or orange-brown scales, slightly viscid in damp weather', but not glutinous, spores 5.5-7.5(-8.0) x (3.0-)3.5-4.3(-4.5) µm , cystidia on lamellae surface and lamellae edge of the same shape. 014333426450 Pholiota lundbergii, pp. 380
0 Growing on living and fallen trunks (main]y Alnus. Betula), pileus golden-yellow, strongly slimy when moist, scales rusty-ochre to rusty-brown, spores 6.5-9.0(-10.0) x 4.0-5.2(-5.5) µm, cystidia on lamellae surface and lamellae edge of different shape. 014333526460 Pholiota limonella, pp. 530
